{"source":"function Unresolved_b6b55f25(uint256 arg0) public view {
        if (0x04 + (msg.data.length - 0x04) - 0x04 >= 0x10) {
            require(uint8(uint256(store_f) / 0x010000000000000000000000000000000000000000) == 0, CustomError_9e87fac8());
            require(arg0 >= uint256(store_c), CustomError_3261c792());
        }
    }","notes":"The probe calls withdraw(100) after setup and the reference succeeds (ok=true, no revert data), while the candidate reverts. The only revert paths in this unit are the two requires and the trailing bare `revert()`, which fires unconditionally after the checks pass. Removing the trailing `revert()` makes the function fall through to a successful return once both checks pass. The checks themselves match the observed state: paused flag (byte 2 of store_f) is 0 since only initialize ran (Unresolved_3f4ba83a/8456cb59 not called), and arg0=100 >= store_c=1 set by setLimits, so both requires pass and the call now succeeds like the reference. No state changes are needed: the reference shows no logs and no balance change for this call, and the subsequent balanceOf/totalSupply reads (0x419 = 1000 minted + 100 deposited - 50 withdrawn... consistent with the separate withdraw unit) are unaffected by this view call."}
